{
  "title": "The Race",
  "arabicTitle": "السباق",
  "level": "B2",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "text": "When Daniel opened his eyes, he had no idea where he was. The bright lights above him hurt his eyes, and a dull pain spread through his head. A nurse hurried over when she saw him awake."
    },
    {
      "text": "“Can you tell me your name?” she asked."
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel stared at her."
    },
    {
      "text": "“I… I don’t know.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "A doctor arrived a few minutes later. He explained that Daniel had been in a serious car accident and had been unconscious for three days. Although he had escaped with only minor injuries, he had lost his memory."
    },
    {
      "text": "“This is called amnesia,” the doctor said. “You may remember everything in a few days, or it could take much longer.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel nodded, but the words meant little to him. He couldn’t even remember his own face."
    },
    {
      "text": "The following afternoon, two detectives visited his room."
    },
    {
      "text": "“I’m Detective Harris, and this is Detective Collins,” the older officer said. “Before your accident, you made an emergency call.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel looked surprised."
    },
    {
      "text": "“I did?”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Harris placed a phone on the bedside table and played a recording."
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel heard his own frightened voice."
    },
    {
      "text": "“Someone’s dead… I saw everything… They’re coming… Please hurry!”"
    },
    {
      "text": "The recording ended with the sound of screeching tyres and a violent crash."
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel felt a chill run through his body."
    },
    {
      "text": "“I don’t remember saying that.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "“We know,” Collins replied. “The problem is that when officers arrived, there was no body. Nothing. It was as if the crime had never happened.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "“So maybe I imagined it.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Harris shook his head."
    },
    {
      "text": "“You sounded terrified. We think you witnessed something real.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "That night Daniel struggled to sleep. Every time he closed his eyes, strange images flashed through his mind. Rain. Trees. A broken window. Someone shouting."
    },
    {
      "text": "Then he saw a hand."
    },
    {
      "text": "The hand was covered in blood."
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel sat upright, breathing heavily. The image disappeared before he could see the person’s face."
    },
    {
      "text": "Over the next week, the detectives visited regularly. They showed him photographs of places near the road where his accident had happened."
    },
    {
      "text": "One picture made him stop."
    },
    {
      "text": "“That building,” he whispered."
    },
    {
      "text": "It was an old warehouse."
    },
    {
      "text": "“I’ve been there.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "The detectives exchanged a quick glance."
    },
    {
      "text": "“Are you sure?”"
    },
    {
      "text": "“I don’t know… but it feels familiar.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Police searched the warehouse the next morning. It had been abandoned for years. Apart from broken furniture and empty boxes, they found nothing."
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel was disappointed. Once again, the clues had disappeared."
    },
    {
      "text": "Then another memory returned."
    },
    {
      "text": "He remembered hiding behind a stack of wooden crates."
    },
    {
      "text": "He remembered hearing two men arguing."
    },
    {
      "text": "One of them had a snake tattoo on his neck."
    },
    {
      "text": "Before Daniel could remember anything else, the memory faded."
    },
    {
      "text": "The detectives checked police records. Only one local criminal was known for having a large snake tattoo."
    },
    {
      "text": "His name was Victor Kane."
    },
    {
      "text": "But when officers searched Kane’s house, he had already vanished."
    },
    {
      "text": "Two days later, Daniel noticed something strange."
    },
    {
      "text": "A man wearing a dark jacket was standing across the street from the hospital."
    },
    {
      "text": "He wasn’t looking at the entrance."
    },
    {
      "text": "He was looking directly at Daniel’s window."
    },
    {
      "text": "When Daniel pointed him out, the man walked away without turning around."
    },
    {
      "text": "The detectives took the sighting seriously. They moved Daniel to another hospital under a different name and placed officers outside his room."
    },
    {
      "text": "“If someone is watching you,” Harris explained, “it’s because they’re afraid you’ll remember.”"
    },
    {
      "text": "That night Daniel had his clearest memory yet."
    },
    {
      "text": "He saw Victor Kane arguing with another man inside the warehouse. Suddenly Kane pushed him. The man fell backwards, hit his head on a metal beam and stopped moving."
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel had pulled out his phone and taken a photograph."
    },
    {
      "text": "Kane had seen the flash."
    },
    {
      "text": "Then he had shouted, “Get him!”"
    },
    {
      "text": "Daniel remembered running to his car before making the emergency call."
    },
    {
      "text": "The next morning, police searched Daniel’s damaged phone again."
    },
    {
      "text": "Hidden inside its memory, forensic experts found the missing photograph."
    },
    {
      "text": "Although blurry, it clearly showed Victor Kane standing over the victim’s body."
    },
    {
      "text": "The evidence was enough."
    },
    {
      "text": "Later that day, police arrested Kane as he tried to leave the country using a false passport."
    },
    {
      "text": "Months later, Daniel’s memory had improved, but parts of that night were still missing. Some memories, the doctors said, might never return."
    },
    {
      "text": "That no longer worried him."
    },
    {
      "text": "He had forgotten many things, but he had remembered the one detail that mattered."
    },
    {
      "text": "Sometimes, a single memory is enough to uncover the truth."
    }
  ],
